DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At maganda naman ang resulta ng ating programa because doon sa 6.7 million na pumasok po sa ARAL program,

asr-000735
00:42:05.930 --> 00:42:13.910
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: we saw at the end of the school year, mayroong 4.5 million fewer struggling readers, at saka may 2.5 million doon sa 6.7 million

asr-000736
00:42:13.930 --> 00:42:20.030
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: na umangat po sa grade level reading, so they are now reading at the right level.

asr-000737
00:42:20.550 --> 00:42:31.790
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So these are a few of the achievements, at sa mga naikutan kong mga eskwelahan, iyon din ang kinukuwento po ng mga teachers at saka principals na effective po yung ARAL program.

asr-000738
00:42:31.990 --> 00:42:40.410
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So again, nagpapasalamat po tayo sa Kongreso sa magandang batas na ito, at hopefully mapagbigyan dito sa mga requests, Your Honor.

asr-000739
00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:43.690
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you, Secretary, for that

asr-000740
00:42:43.930 --> 00:42:44.690
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: response.

asr-000741
00:42:45.590 --> 00:42:47.490
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Pangalawa po, Madam Chair.

asr-000742
00:42:48.810 --> 00:42:58.950
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Sapat ba ito, Secretary, to cover the whole program and the remuneration of teachers, para-teachers, who will serve as ARAL tutors.

asr-000743
00:42:59.570 --> 00:43:02.610
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: I believe this covers reading, math, and science.

asr-000744
00:43:03.550 --> 00:43:08.850
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Also, these teachers are already carrying a tremendous workload in our public schools.

asr-000745
00:43:08.850 --> 00:43:13.110
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: If we are asking them to provide additional tutoring,

asr-000746
00:43:13.930 --> 00:43:20.470
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: beyond their regular responsibilities, we must ensure that their regular responsibilities,

asr-000747
00:43:20.470 --> 00:43:25.570
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: we must ensure that they are properly and fairly compensated.

asr-000748
00:43:25.570 --> 00:43:36.290
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Madam Chair, Secretary, we cannot ask our teachers to close the learning gaps of our children while leaving a gap in the support we give to our teachers.

asr-000749
00:43:36.290 --> 00:43:38.290
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Thank you, Madam Chair, Secretary.

asr-000750
00:43:38.290 --> 00:43:40.870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Madam Chair, thank you for the question.

asr-000751
00:43:40.870 --> 00:43:42.770
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasama po sa request namin iyon, yung remuneration

asr-000754
00:43:43.790 --> 00:43:46.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ng ARAL teachers and tutors, Your Honor.

asr-000755
00:43:46.850 --> 00:43:51.290
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 3.5 billion ang total remuneration na ni-request po namin.

asr-000756
00:43:51.290 --> 00:43:52.770
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Kasya na ba ito?

asr-000757
00:43:53.130 --> 00:43:56.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasya na po.

asr-000758
00:43:56.430 --> 00:43:57.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasya na po iyon, Your Honor.

asr-000759
00:43:58.210 --> 00:44:00.970
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Salamat po sa inyong tugon, Secretary.

asr-000760
00:44:00.970 --> 00:44:08.550
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Madam Chair and Secretary, may I manifest my support to allocate appropriate funding needed by DepEd

asr-000761
00:44:08.550 --> 00:44:11.150
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: to successfully implement the ARAL program.

asr-000762
00:44:11.150 --> 00:44:13.150
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: It should be our priority to help our Filipino children to catch up,

asr-000763
00:44:13.490 --> 00:44:14.590
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: learn better

asr-000764
00:44:15.930 --> 00:44:17.830
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: and regain their confidence

asr-000765
00:44:17.830 --> 00:44:19.150
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: in their own abilities.

asr-000766
00:44:19.490 --> 00:44:21.390
Rep. Salvador A. Pleyto: Thank you, Madam Chair. Thank you, Secretary.

asr-000767
00:44:22.030 --> 00:44:23.050
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming salamat,

asr-000768
00:44:23.650 --> 00:44:25.170
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Congressman Pleyto, Madam Chair.

asr-000769
00:44:25.550 --> 00:44:26.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Salamat po sa support.

asr-000770
00:44:27.650 --> 00:44:28.930
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Thank you very much.

asr-000771
00:44:29.730 --> 00:44:31.850
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Next to us, question is from the minority.

asr-000772
00:44:32.690 --> 00:44:33.650
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The Chair acknowledges

asr-000773
00:44:33.650 --> 00:44:35.630
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Edgar

asr-000774
00:44:35.630 --> 00:44:37.430
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Erice.

asr-000774-split-2
00:44:37.430 --> 00:44:39.150
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Magandang

asr-000775
00:44:39.150 --> 00:44:41.270
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: umaga po, Madam Chair,

asr-000776
00:44:41.410 --> 00:44:42.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: sa ating kalihim,

asr-000777
00:44:43.190 --> 00:44:44.350
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: magaling na kalihim ng

asr-000778
00:44:44.350 --> 00:44:47.210
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Department of Education. Alam ko po na

asr-000779
00:44:47.210 --> 00:44:49.310
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: very capable at napakagaling

asr-000780
00:44:49.310 --> 00:44:50.570
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ng kalihim ng

asr-000781
00:44:50.570 --> 00:44:52.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Department of Education.

asr-000782
00:44:53.730 --> 00:44:55.170
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Subalit, ano kaya

asr-000783
00:44:55.170 --> 00:44:56.450
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: magagawa ng

asr-000784
00:44:56.450 --> 00:44:59.570
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ating kalihim kung napakalaki

asr-000785
00:44:59.570 --> 00:45:00.000
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ng bawas

asr-000786
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.000
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ng kanyang budget.

asr-000787
00:45:02.300 --> 00:45:09.460
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Nakita, kung napansin ko po sa basic education, facilities, negative 64.2%.

asr-000788
00:45:09.460 --> 00:45:17.020
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Government assistance to senior high school voucher program, 100%. Wala po.

asr-000789
00:45:17.900 --> 00:45:21.940
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: School-based feeding program, negative 55%.

asr-000790
00:45:21.940 --> 00:45:29.060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Textbook and other instructional materials, negative 66.8%.

asr-000791
00:45:29.060 --> 00:45:32.120
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: This is compared to the 2026 GAA.

asr-000792
00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:42.000
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Government assistance and subsidies, educational service contracting program for private junior high school, 100%.

asr-000793
00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:43.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Wala na po. Zero.

asr-000794
00:45:43.980 --> 00:45:47.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: New school personal positions, negative 25%.

asr-000795
00:45:48.760 --> 00:45:58.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Para sa infrastructure for safer and resilient schools, a project of the World Bank, negative 75%.

asr-000796
00:45:59.060 --> 00:46:05.140
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Computerization program, negative 45%.

asr-000797
00:46:05.140 --> 00:46:09.280
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Basic education curriculum, negative 50%.

asr-000798
00:46:09.280 --> 00:46:14.040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: School innovation and improvement fund, negative, wala na, zero.

asr-000799
00:46:14.940 --> 00:46:21.740
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Joint delivery voucher for senior high school, technical, vocational, and livelihood specialization, zero na rin po.

asr-000800
00:46:22.220 --> 00:46:24.920
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Anong po ba ang ibig sabihin nito? Maraming pang iba.

asr-000801
00:46:27.540 --> 00:46:30.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair, Congressman.

asr-000802
00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:33.260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you very much for the kind words you mentioned.

asr-000803
00:46:33.820 --> 00:46:36.040
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero tama po kayo, malaki po ang bawas sa budget.

asr-000804
00:46:37.040 --> 00:46:44.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero nantindihan din po natin yung konteksto ng malaking budget ng 2026 na bunga din po,

asr-000805
00:46:44.420 --> 00:46:53.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: kumbaga bonanza ng flood control dahil yung 200 billion na napunta po sa edukasyon at health.

asr-000806
00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:55.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And hopefully, magpatuloy po.

asr-000807
00:46:55.780 --> 00:47:00.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, tama po kayo na nawala po yung mga pondong yun.

asr-000808
00:47:00.600 --> 00:47:09.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And so, yung sa feeding, for example, nag-request po kami ng additional para ma-maintain lang po yung this year's level.

asr-000809
00:47:09.820 --> 00:47:17.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi this year, aside from universal kindergarten o lahat ng bata sa kindergarten ay pinapakain, pati grade 1 po.

asr-000810
00:47:18.080 --> 00:47:28.220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, napansin nga ng mga UNICEF at saka ng mga ibang international organizations na yung commitment ng Pilipinas sa foundational learning

asr-000811
00:47:28.220 --> 00:47:29.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and holistic learning.

asr-000812
00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:32.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Holistic approach to learning.

asr-000813
00:47:32.760 --> 00:47:34.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, sana yun, maibalik po.

asr-000814
00:47:35.160 --> 00:47:41.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At kasi ang sakop din po ng feeding ngayon is 120 days under the 2027 budget.

asr-000815
00:47:42.480 --> 00:47:49.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hopefully, ma-extend yun sa 180 days, which is for the current school year or the current fiscal year.

asr-000816
00:47:49.540 --> 00:48:00.460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi nga po, ang napansin namin is, tinitimbang natin yung mga bata at very successful yung feeding dahil,

asr-000817
00:48:00.600 --> 00:48:03.060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they gain weight.

asr-000818
00:48:03.460 --> 00:48:08.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero, pagka meron pong butal or meron pong portion ng school year na hindi sila pinapakain,

asr-000819
00:48:08.840 --> 00:48:10.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: bumabalik din po sa dating tinbang.

asr-000820
00:48:11.180 --> 00:48:18.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And, of course, the evidence is very strong also for improved learning outcomes,

asr-000821
00:48:19.240 --> 00:48:21.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: especially sa younger years.

asr-000822
00:48:21.520 --> 00:48:23.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's why we're focusing on kinder and grade 1.

asr-000823
00:48:23.980 --> 00:48:24.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, sana may balik po yun.

asr-000824
00:48:25.720 --> 00:48:30.560
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Definitely, there's a proven connection or correlation between the feeding and the,

asr-000825
00:48:30.560 --> 00:48:31.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: the learning outcomes, Your Honor.

asr-000826
00:48:31.780 --> 00:48:36.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, that's just one aspect of the many programs that you mentioned.

asr-000827
00:48:36.980 --> 00:48:41.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung aral nga, as mentioned in the interchange with Congressman Plato,

asr-000828
00:48:41.340 --> 00:48:43.880
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: wala rin pondo, allotted funds for that.

asr-000829
00:48:43.880 --> 00:48:50.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, and then, ang gusto nga po natin is ma-expand yung aral program to math and science later on.

asr-000830
00:48:51.100 --> 00:48:54.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil yung nagawa po lang natin is reading, aral reading.

asr-000831
00:48:55.220 --> 00:48:57.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And yet, napakaganda na po nung epekto.

asr-000832
00:48:57.640 --> 00:48:59.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil for the first time in history,

asr-000833
00:48:59.360 --> 00:49:02.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: at nagpapasalamat muli tayo sa Kongreso kay Pangulong Marcos,

asr-000834
00:49:02.880 --> 00:49:07.860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: na merong programa, na merong tutors ang bawat estudyante ng public schools.

asr-000835
00:49:07.980 --> 00:49:09.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: First time nangyari po yan.

asr-000836
00:49:09.520 --> 00:49:16.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I know certain LGUs, certain schools, kumukuha ng sponsor para gawin yun.

asr-000837
00:49:16.820 --> 00:49:19.700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero it's the first time it was done on a system-wide basis.

asr-000838
00:49:19.840 --> 00:49:21.940
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, sana masustain yung momentum na ito.

asr-000839
00:49:21.940 --> 00:49:25.300
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And at the same time, it's also,

asr-000840
00:49:25.300 --> 00:49:31.000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: it's also an incentive, yung school feeding is also an incentive for attendance.

asr-000841
00:49:31.320 --> 00:49:35.760
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nakita natin, nag-improve din po yung attendance ng mga bata sa eskwelahan.

asr-000842
00:49:35.760 --> 00:49:41.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, these are just two of the aspects of the, of, tapos yung voucher program,

asr-000843
00:49:41.620 --> 00:49:46.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi naman na zero yung voucher program.

asr-000844
00:49:46.800 --> 00:49:48.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ano lang, nabawasan lang ng konti.

asr-000845
00:49:48.440 --> 00:49:50.540
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, that means less beneficiaries also.

asr-000846
00:49:51.080 --> 00:49:57.180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And as we know, the voucher program is also one way of decongesting

asr-000847
00:49:57.180 --> 00:49:57.320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: our congested public schools

asr-000848
00:49:57.340 --> 00:50:03.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: by giving vouchers to nearby private schools in the area

asr-000849
00:50:03.720 --> 00:50:09.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: para mabawasan po ng class size yung ating mga ibang public school, Your Honor.

asr-000850
00:50:09.680 --> 00:50:14.340
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa data ko po, Secretary, 26 billion ng 2026.

asr-000851
00:50:15.100 --> 00:50:15.800
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ngayon po, zero.

asr-000852
00:50:18.990 --> 00:50:23.550
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It was just consolidated, kaya siguro magmukhang nagbago ho.

asr-000853
00:50:23.550 --> 00:50:28.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But it's consolidated, the consolidated program including the,

asr-000854
00:50:28.370 --> 00:50:32.150
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: the JDVP, the ESC, amounts to 38 billion,

asr-000855
00:50:32.290 --> 00:50:35.890
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which is a decrease of around 3 billion from last year, Your Honor.

asr-000856
00:50:38.420 --> 00:50:43.240
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Secretary, nabawasan din po ng negative din po yung government assistance and subsidies

asr-000857
00:50:43.240 --> 00:50:45.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: for educational services.

asr-000858
00:50:45.800 --> 00:50:46.500
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Zero na rin po.

asr-000859
00:50:48.720 --> 00:50:51.980
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yan po, nabawasan ng 3 billion ho yung programang sinasabi din nyo, Your Honor.

asr-000860
00:50:55.520 --> 00:50:59.240
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Secretary, alam nyo, ito po yung mga planado na yung programa.

asr-000861
00:51:00.020 --> 00:51:03.620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meron na pong, gumugulong na itong programa, madaling ang implementation.

asr-000862
00:51:03.620 --> 00:51:08.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: May 58 billion for LGSF.

asr-000863
00:51:09.140 --> 00:51:09.780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Billion.

asr-000864
00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:13.200
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ito po, 10 billion lang.

asr-000865
00:51:13.620 --> 00:51:19.800
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe you can suggest to the President that bawasan na yung 58 billion na LGSF,

asr-000866
00:51:19.860 --> 00:51:20.900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: na wala naman talaga.

asr-000867
00:51:21.460 --> 00:51:22.880
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Wala pang plano.

asr-000868
00:51:24.220 --> 00:51:29.480
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pag-aalatsamba pa tayo doon, dito meron na talaga para sa mga kabataan.

asr-000869
00:51:29.480 --> 00:51:32.420
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So maybe Congress can also consider that.

asr-000870
00:51:32.840 --> 00:51:33.260
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kasi po,

asr-000871
00:51:33.620 --> 00:51:35.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: kawawa naman yung mga kabataan natin.

asr-000872
00:51:36.500 --> 00:51:36.780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And,

asr-000873
00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:41.740
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: parami pong pangako ang Pangulo sa edukasyon.

asr-000874
00:51:42.040 --> 00:51:43.540
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ayan po, nilista ko lahat.

asr-000875
00:51:44.380 --> 00:51:47.280
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Tutugunan ang kakulangan at kondisyon ng mga silid-aralan.

asr-000876
00:51:48.740 --> 00:51:50.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Hindi pa rin po masyadong na-implement.

asr-000877
00:51:51.960 --> 00:51:56.680
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Magtatayo ng 40,000 classrooms bago matapos ang termino sa 2028.

asr-000878
00:51:56.840 --> 00:51:57.700
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kaya pa po ba ito?

asr-000879
00:52:00.950 --> 00:52:01.670
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Classrooms, o?

asr-000880
00:52:01.790 --> 00:52:02.350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Classrooms?

asr-000881
00:52:02.350 --> 00:52:02.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes.

asr-000882
00:52:02.990 --> 00:52:06.090
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meron pong pangako na magtatayo ng 40,000 classrooms.

asr-000883
00:52:06.110 --> 00:52:08.670
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bago matapos ang termino sa 2028.

asr-000884
00:52:08.910 --> 00:52:09.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kaya pa po ito?

asr-000885
00:52:09.950 --> 00:52:10.110
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Okay.

asr-000886
00:52:11.950 --> 00:52:15.590
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, you know, on the average, Madam Chair, Your Honor,

asr-000887
00:52:16.170 --> 00:52:21.770
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ang napafun ho nang ga-a for classrooms is around 5,000 approximately per year.

asr-000888
00:52:22.770 --> 00:52:27.230
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero for this year, because dito nga sa historic budget na binigay ninyo po sa amin,

asr-000889
00:52:27.770 --> 00:52:32.630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: we have around 60 billion for infra classrooms, new classrooms.

asr-000890
00:52:32.630 --> 00:52:35.630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, that will...

asr-000891
00:52:36.110 --> 00:52:42.960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: represent around 18,000 classrooms, Your Honor.

asr-000892
00:52:43.140 --> 00:52:46.720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tapos meron ding sinasalang na PPP or Public-Private Partnership,

asr-000893
00:52:47.500 --> 00:52:52.360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which na-approve na ho ng NEDA or DepDev ICC,

asr-000894
00:52:53.180 --> 00:52:54.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung...

asr-000895
00:52:54.520 --> 00:52:56.920
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: How many?

asr-000896
00:52:57.700 --> 00:52:59.380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Another 16,000, ho.

asr-000897
00:52:59.680 --> 00:53:04.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, dito pa lang sa taong ito, ma-umpisahan na ho siguro yung 34,000.

asr-000898
00:53:04.480 --> 00:53:08.480
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, it's still a long way towards the...

asr-000899
00:53:09.120 --> 00:53:15.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 140 plus thousand classroom deficit that we have accumulated over the years.

asr-000900
00:53:15.700 --> 00:53:25.660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But definitely, it is the biggest attempt to make a dent or to improve upon the classroom deficit.

asr-000901
00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:31.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, kumbaga hindi siya business as usual, Your Honor, Mr. President.

asr-000902
00:53:31.120 --> 00:53:38.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Madam Chair, talagang nag-i-effort si Pangulo and ang member ng Kongreso to solve this...

asr-000903
00:53:39.120 --> 00:53:42.640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: years-old problem, Kong Egay.

asr-000904
00:53:43.240 --> 00:53:45.180
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, thank you, Secretary.

asr-000905
00:53:45.740 --> 00:53:48.880
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa distrito ko po, mga 150 classrooms lang kukulang.

asr-000906
00:53:49.380 --> 00:53:53.620
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Talagang bago mag-2028, baka matupad ni Pangulo sa kanyang pangako.

asr-000907
00:53:53.760 --> 00:53:54.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa kalookan man lang.

asr-000908
00:53:57.220 --> 00:53:58.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will do that, Your Honor.

asr-000909
00:54:00.200 --> 00:54:03.040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bibigyan ng laptop ang bawat public school teacher.

asr-000910
00:54:06.080 --> 00:54:08.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, this year, we're giving...

asr-000911
00:54:10.120 --> 00:54:11.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think over 200,000...

asr-000912
00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:18.170
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 283,000 laptops, which, again, is not business as usual, Your Honor.

asr-000913
00:54:18.270 --> 00:54:21.330
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We have about 870,000 teachers.

asr-000914
00:54:21.810 --> 00:54:26.070
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: This is the biggest single allocation in any year for our teachers.

asr-000915
00:54:26.730 --> 00:54:28.790
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, again, the question is sustainability.

asr-000916
00:54:29.610 --> 00:54:33.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil kung hindi natin masustain ito, hindi natin mabibigyan lahat.

asr-000917
00:54:33.370 --> 00:54:38.570
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But definitely, in one year, we're giving almost one-third of the school teachers already.

asr-000918
00:54:41.190 --> 00:54:45.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, by end of the term, the President, kaya-kayang mabibigyan?

asr-000919
00:54:45.070 --> 00:54:48.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Lahat ng laptop, yung mga teachers?

asr-000920
00:54:49.730 --> 00:54:54.890
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa 2027 budget, there's funding only for 50,000 laptops, Your Honor.

asr-000921
00:54:56.130 --> 00:55:02.330
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's why we're requesting an additional 10B para ma-fulfill po yung pangako niya.

asr-000922
00:55:03.630 --> 00:55:10.770
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: How about yung pangako po na yung lowering of learning poverty para po sa ating basic education?

asr-000923
00:55:11.670 --> 00:55:12.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ano na po ba ang improvement?

asr-000924
00:55:12.750 --> 00:55:14.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: For example, in the...

asr-000925
00:55:15.070 --> 00:55:31.570
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, this week, hopefully, we will be getting some good news.

asr-000926
00:55:31.730 --> 00:55:37.650
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But we'll have to wait because the results of these exams are embargoed, Your Honor, until tomorrow.

asr-000927
00:55:39.170 --> 00:55:39.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Hanggang bukas po.

asr-000928
00:55:39.970 --> 00:55:40.270
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Opo.

asr-000929
00:55:40.270 --> 00:55:44.150
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil iuunang ng OECD yung pag-release po ng impormasyon.

asr-000930
00:55:44.150 --> 00:55:59.970
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kasi po, yung OECD standards, nung mga nakaraan, nasa mga 69% yung average sa mga kabataan sa buong mundo,

asr-000931
00:56:00.910 --> 00:56:08.170
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: tayo po, napakalayo natin. Hopefully, tomorrow, we will hear good news.

asr-000932
00:56:08.750 --> 00:56:09.910
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor. Hopefully.

asr-000933
00:56:09.910 --> 00:56:13.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because the department has really been making an effort.

asr-000934
00:56:13.490 --> 00:56:14.010
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At mismo si Pangulo.

asr-000935
00:56:14.150 --> 00:56:19.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nung bagong appoint sa akin, sinabi niya na dapat pagbudihin po natin yung performance natin dyan.

asr-000936
00:56:19.950 --> 00:56:26.950
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At you're right. In 2018, we were the last of all the countries, I think of about 60 plus countries who participated.

asr-000937
00:56:27.410 --> 00:56:30.910
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In 2022, we were third from the last of all the countries.

asr-000938
00:56:31.190 --> 00:56:32.150
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, hopefully...

asr-000939
00:56:32.810 --> 00:56:39.050
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hopefully, wala na tayo sa third, second, at last.

asr-000940
00:56:39.410 --> 00:56:40.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Anyway, anyway po.

asr-000941
00:56:40.910 --> 00:56:43.670
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, pagdating naman po sa mga textbooks.

asr-000942
00:56:44.150 --> 00:56:47.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And materials. Ano po ba ang improvement natin dyan?

asr-000943
00:56:48.190 --> 00:56:56.010
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Again, Madam Chair, there is a historic allocation of over 20 billion for textbooks this year.

asr-000944
00:56:56.010 --> 00:57:06.550
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung pangarap po natin is, yung naabutan po kasi namin, yung isang textbook ay sineshare at pinapasa ng apat na batches ng mga bata.

asr-000945
00:57:06.970 --> 00:57:13.130
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kaya sinasabihan yung bata, huwag sulatan yung textbook, huwag iuwi dahil ipapasa pa niya yun.

asr-000946
00:57:13.130 --> 00:57:18.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, minsan, kung ikaw yung fourth batch, ang nakuha mo na ay warak-warak na po na libro.

asr-000947
00:57:18.790 --> 00:57:23.510
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, ang goal talaga natin is one textbook, one learner, your honor.

asr-000948
00:57:23.610 --> 00:57:27.350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we're on our way to meet that, so definitely, it is not business as usual.

asr-000949
00:57:28.070 --> 00:57:36.090
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At nadagdagan din po natin yung supplementary learning materials, which is not just the textbooks na dun sa mga klase ng mga bata.

asr-000950
00:57:36.390 --> 00:57:40.010
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pati yung mga libro na nasa library, at pwede silang iuwi-iwi ito.

asr-000951
00:57:40.010 --> 00:57:42.010
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil dati, hindi na iuwi ito dahil...

asr-000952
00:57:43.130 --> 00:57:46.330
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Saka teacher pag nawawala, so ayaw na teacher pa uwi.

asr-000953
00:57:46.450 --> 00:57:48.610
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero ngayon, hindi na natin ganun ang polisiya.

asr-000954
00:57:48.930 --> 00:57:53.910
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: They're free to bring it home and they're free to write also.

asr-000955
00:57:54.130 --> 00:58:02.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're encouraging them to write because there are studies which show that writing, handwriting aids memory retention, your honor.

asr-000956
00:58:02.530 --> 00:58:06.790
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's one of the biggest studies which came out recently.

asr-000957
00:58:07.350 --> 00:58:10.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, these are some of the developments in textbooks, your honor.

asr-000958
00:58:10.370 --> 00:58:12.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At dati...

asr-000959
00:58:13.130 --> 00:58:21.330
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ang finding ng EDCOM, a little over parang 20, 27 textbooks in the last 10 years ang na-procure.

asr-000960
00:58:21.970 --> 00:58:27.770
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In 2026, we procured 105 out of 105 titles, your honor.

asr-000961
00:58:28.090 --> 00:58:30.350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ang challenge na lang namin is i-deliver on time.

asr-000962
00:58:30.650 --> 00:58:31.870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dati nalilate ng one year.

asr-000963
00:58:32.190 --> 00:58:35.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Siguro ngayon, malate na lang kami ng linggo o buwan na lang po.

asr-000964
00:58:35.250 --> 00:58:41.770
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yun. Pero I think before 2028, makuha na natin yun because we are working on early procurement, your honor.

asr-000965
00:58:43.130 --> 00:58:45.410
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, 37 seconds na lang ako.

asr-000966
00:58:45.950 --> 00:58:47.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Hindi ko na ubusin.

asr-000967
00:58:48.130 --> 00:58:49.410
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: One last question.

asr-000968
00:58:50.070 --> 00:58:58.390
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alam nyo, ang pinakamalaking problema ng education actually sa aking research, sa aking distrito,

asr-000969
00:59:00.230 --> 00:59:04.970
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ay yung parents, they're not so interested in the education of their children.

asr-000970
00:59:04.970 --> 00:59:07.970
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe because of poverty, maybe because of other...

asr-000971
00:59:08.870 --> 00:59:12.970
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Meron po bang DepEd na parang intervention?

asr-000972
00:59:13.130 --> 00:59:16.930
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: When it comes to parenting dito sa ating mga...

asr-000973
00:59:16.930 --> 00:59:19.150
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Especially in the elementary school.

asr-000974
00:59:21.150 --> 00:59:24.670
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you. Napakagandang tanong ho, [unclear].

asr-000975
00:59:25.990 --> 00:59:31.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Negative apps or websites that have a negative influence on him.

asr-000976
00:59:31.490 --> 00:59:35.290
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, this has led many countries, in fact, to impose social media bans, your honor.

asr-000977
00:59:36.230 --> 00:59:39.350
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maraming salamat po and congratulations to the DepEd family.

asr-000978
00:59:39.610 --> 00:59:41.070
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming salamat sa inyo, Kong Egy.

asr-000979
00:59:41.070 --> 00:59:42.970
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Madam Chair, thank you.

asr-000980
00:59:43.130 --> 00:59:45.290
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Thank you very much, Congressman Erice.

asr-000981
00:59:45.470 --> 00:59:52.990
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Before we proceed to the next member, last question, allow me to recognize the presence of the following members.

asr-000982
00:59:53.530 --> 00:59:59.210
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Vice Chairperson Gerardo "Gerryboy" J. Espina Jr., Representative Elmer V. Catulpos.

asr-000983
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:03.380
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Vice Chairperson John Geesnell "Baba" Yap,

asr-000984
01:00:04.220 --> 01:00:07.180
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Antonino B. Roman III,

asr-000985
01:00:08.100 --> 01:00:11.300
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Lani Mercado-Revilla,

asr-000986
01:00:11.820 --> 01:00:14.340
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Ricardo S. Cruz Jr.,

asr-000987
01:00:15.180 --> 01:00:17.660
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Vice Chairperson Bernadette S. Barbers,

asr-000988
01:00:18.220 --> 01:00:20.620
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Caroline B. Agyao,

asr-000989
01:00:20.620 --> 01:00:24.120
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Shirlyn L. Bañas-Nograles,

asr-000990
01:00:24.600 --> 01:00:26.940
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Sergio C. Dagooc,

asr-000991
01:00:26.940 --> 01:00:30.920
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Edsel A. Galeos,

asr-000992
01:00:31.640 --> 01:00:34.120
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Iris Marie Demesa Montes,

asr-000993
01:00:34.800 --> 01:00:36.960
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative Mike Tan,

asr-000994
01:00:40.120 --> 01:00:42.220
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Representative John Chan.

asr-000995
01:00:43.700 --> 01:00:48.600
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Next to ask a question is Representative Adrian Michael A. Amatong.

asr-000996
01:00:51.430 --> 01:00:53.030
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Thank you very much Madam Chair.

asr-000997
01:00:53.210 --> 01:00:55.430
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Magandang umaga po sa buong DepEd family.

asr-000998
01:00:55.930 --> 01:00:57.050
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Magandang umaga po sa lahat.

asr-000999
01:00:57.730 --> 01:01:00.070
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Maraming salamat po Secretary at sa buong DepEd

asr-001000
01:01:00.070 --> 01:01:01.370
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: sa lahat ng mga ginagawa niyo.

asr-001001
01:01:01.390 --> 01:01:04.730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kanina nga nabanggit niyo yung mga record figures

asr-001002
01:01:04.730 --> 01:01:06.110
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: dun sa mga sa classroom,

asr-001003
01:01:06.550 --> 01:01:08.630
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: sa mga at saka pinamamahagi niyo ng mga materials.

asr-001004
01:01:09.330 --> 01:01:10.550
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Thank you for your efforts.

asr-001005
01:01:11.310 --> 01:01:12.730
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Unfortunately, sabi niyo nga,

asr-001006
01:01:13.210 --> 01:01:13.870
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: hindi pa enough.

asr-001007
01:01:14.050 --> 01:01:14.770
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Marami pang kulang.

asr-001008
01:01:15.090 --> 01:01:17.410
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: At least, unti-unti na atutugunan natin.

asr-001009
01:01:18.190 --> 01:01:21.150
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Representing a poverty stricken district and province,

asr-001010
01:01:22.130 --> 01:01:23.870
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: malaking bagay po sa amin yung sitwasyon

asr-001011
01:01:23.870 --> 01:01:25.390
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: ng classroom shortage.

asr-001012
01:01:26.730 --> 01:01:27.610
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Lalo sa distrito ko,

asr-001013
01:01:28.210 --> 01:01:30.390
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: more than 700 pa yung shortage namin.

asr-001014
01:01:30.390 --> 01:01:31.250
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Tapos yung needing

asr-001015
01:01:31.390 --> 01:01:32.750
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: minor and major repairs,

asr-001016
01:01:32.750 --> 01:01:33.950
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: more than a thousand.

asr-001017
01:01:33.950 --> 01:01:35.950
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Gusto lang po naman kung ano yung updates

asr-001018
01:01:35.950 --> 01:01:37.950
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: tungkol doon sa classrooms.

asr-001019
01:01:39.630 --> 01:01:44.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We have signed MOAS with

asr-001020
01:01:44.430 --> 01:01:47.970
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: about over 350 local government units,

asr-001021
01:01:47.970 --> 01:01:48.710
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

asr-001022
01:01:48.710 --> 01:01:52.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Representing over 20 billion pesos worth of classrooms.

asr-001023
01:01:52.390 --> 01:01:54.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tapos yung

asr-001024
01:01:54.390 --> 01:01:58.050
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: nabigay na rin po namin yung validated lists of

asr-001025
01:01:58.050 --> 01:02:09.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ang good news siguro is that

asr-001026
01:02:09.580 --> 01:02:13.420
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: the next batch of public-private partnership

asr-001027
01:02:13.420 --> 01:02:15.780
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: will have a big focus on Mindanao.

asr-001028
01:02:15.900 --> 01:02:18.620
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So we'll make sure that your district is included

asr-001029
01:02:18.620 --> 01:02:21.440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: because 700 is a big backlog for one district,

asr-001030
01:02:21.560 --> 01:02:21.800
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

asr-001031
01:02:22.260 --> 01:02:23.520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At we acknowledge that

asr-001032
01:02:23.520 --> 01:02:26.120
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Zamboanga Peninsula is one of the

asr-001033
01:02:26.120 --> 01:02:28.600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: most poverty stricken areas of our country

asr-001034
01:02:28.600 --> 01:02:30.020
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and we will make an effort to

asr-001035
01:02:30.020 --> 01:02:32.900
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: really improve the educational situation there.

asr-001036
01:02:33.360 --> 01:02:35.240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Given that you don't have many cities,

asr-001037
01:02:35.580 --> 01:02:37.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi mayayaman yung mga LGUs doon.

asr-001038
01:02:37.280 --> 01:02:39.280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So talagang, you're very reliant on national

asr-001039
01:02:39.580 --> 01:02:41.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: government support.

asr-001040
01:02:41.580 --> 01:02:43.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We acknowledge that, Your Honor.

asr-001041
01:02:43.580 --> 01:02:47.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we will take that into account in the funding of classrooms in the future, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

asr-001042
01:02:49.580 --> 01:02:52.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Knowing fully yung problema natin sa classrooms,

asr-001043
01:02:52.580 --> 01:02:55.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: thankful tayo na maraming ginagawa.

asr-001044
01:02:55.580 --> 01:02:59.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Pwede po kayang ma-increase natin yung budget natin for repairs of classrooms?

asr-001045
01:02:59.580 --> 01:03:02.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi minsan may mga classrooms na needing repair,

asr-001046
01:03:02.580 --> 01:03:05.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: eh pag hindi natin ni-repair, eh tutuloy lang masisira yun.

asr-001047
01:03:05.580 --> 01:03:07.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So magco-construct naman tayo ng bago.

asr-001048
01:03:07.580 --> 01:03:09.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Since mas mura naman mag-repair,

asr-001049
01:03:09.580 --> 01:03:13.580
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: lalong-lalo na po sa mga poverty stricken na mga provinces.

asr-001050
01:03:15.580 --> 01:03:18.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maganda po yung puntos ninyo, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

asr-001051
01:03:18.580 --> 01:03:22.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi madalas nababanggit yung backlog sa classrooms.

asr-001052
01:03:22.580 --> 01:03:26.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero may backlog din tayo sa repairs.

asr-001053
01:03:26.580 --> 01:03:29.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In fact, the backlog for repairs is probably more than the...

asr-001054
01:03:29.580 --> 01:03:30.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And why is that?

asr-001055
01:03:30.580 --> 01:03:34.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because many of our classrooms are over 50 years old already.

asr-001056
01:03:34.580 --> 01:03:37.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kumbaga past the use date already.

asr-001057
01:03:37.580 --> 01:03:39.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So pinagamit na lang natin dahil wala tayong...

asr-001058
01:03:39.580 --> 01:03:43.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pinagtsatsaga na lang po natin dahil wala pa po yung bagong classroom.

asr-001059
01:03:43.580 --> 01:03:46.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So tama po kayo kung pwede po madagdagan.

asr-001060
01:03:46.580 --> 01:03:48.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Again, for this year, napakagandang budget po.

asr-001061
01:03:48.580 --> 01:03:51.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think we had about 6 or 7 billion for repairs.

asr-001062
01:03:51.580 --> 01:03:53.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So marami po tayong na-repair.

asr-001063
01:03:53.580 --> 01:03:56.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But I think for 2027...

asr-001064
01:03:58.580 --> 01:04:00.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: There's 5 billion for the budget, Your Honor.

asr-001065
01:04:00.580 --> 01:04:02.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So that's still higher than previous years, Your Honor.

asr-001066
01:04:02.580 --> 01:04:05.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Where ang budget for repairs was just a few billion.

asr-001067
01:04:05.580 --> 01:04:08.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So kung madagdagan pa ho, we would welcome that.

asr-001068
01:04:08.580 --> 01:04:14.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Because as mentioned, talagang hindi napapansin masyado yung repairs deficit actually.

asr-001069
01:04:14.580 --> 01:04:20.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Where we are holding off on condemning school buildings which already should be condemned.

asr-001070
01:04:20.580 --> 01:04:23.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And perhaps are not as safe as they should be.

asr-001071
01:04:23.580 --> 01:04:27.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kung tinamaan po tayo ng mga sakuna, like nilindol po tayo,

asr-001072
01:04:27.580 --> 01:04:35.580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: baka we will have unintended consequences, Your Honor, Madam Chair.

asr-001073
01:04:35.580 --> 01:04:44.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Madam Chair, isa sa mga problema namin, being very far from Metro Manila,

asr-001074
01:04:44.930 --> 01:04:47.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: is yung mga materials natin dun sa amin, ang tagal dumating.

asr-001075
01:04:47.930 --> 01:04:53.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So minsan, kawawa yung mga estudyante, medyo dehado na nga sa infrastructure.

asr-001076
01:04:53.930 --> 01:04:57.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Dun ba sa learning materials, minsan ang tagal-tagal pang dumating.

asr-001077
01:04:57.930 --> 01:04:59.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Baka po pwedeng ma-address natin?

asr-001078
01:04:59.930 --> 01:05:02.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor. We're undertaking early procurement.

asr-001079
01:05:02.930 --> 01:05:05.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And as mentioned, we've closed the gap in procuring textbooks.

asr-001080
01:05:05.930 --> 01:05:09.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're trying to close the gap in delivering textbooks on time, Your Honor.

asr-001081
01:05:09.930 --> 01:05:13.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero dati, buwan at saka taon ang delay sa textbooks.

asr-001082
01:05:13.930 --> 01:05:16.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ngayon, linggo na lang. Pero unacceptable pa rin ho ito.

asr-001083
01:05:16.930 --> 01:05:20.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We acknowledge and we will strive to do better, Your Honor.

asr-001084
01:05:20.930 --> 01:05:25.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Last po, yung ano, meron po ba tayong program yung sa...

asr-001085
01:05:25.930 --> 01:05:29.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi mga teachers natin, karamihan, although pinataasan natin yung sahod,

asr-001086
01:05:29.930 --> 01:05:33.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: eh lagi namang problema natin yung sa mga pautang.

asr-001087
01:05:33.930 --> 01:05:34.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So yung meron po ba tayong program yung sa...

asr-001088
01:05:34.930 --> 01:05:38.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: So yung meron ba tayong program para ma-educate yung teachers natin?

asr-001089
01:05:38.930 --> 01:05:44.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, meron po tayong financial literacy programs that we encourage teachers.

asr-001090
01:05:44.930 --> 01:05:48.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But of course, every month may trainings po tayo.

asr-001091
01:05:48.930 --> 01:05:50.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero siyempre, yung kultura nandun pa rin.

asr-001092
01:05:50.930 --> 01:05:57.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At saka siyempre, ang kaibahan po ng teacher talagang hindi lang mga anak o asawang dependent sa kanya.

asr-001093
01:05:57.930 --> 01:06:02.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pati yung buong angkan, minsan nakaangkas dun sa ating mga guro.

asr-001094
01:06:02.930 --> 01:06:06.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think that's well known to our honorable legislators.

asr-001095
01:06:06.930 --> 01:06:09.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But having said that, we're trying to find ways also.

asr-001096
01:06:09.930 --> 01:06:14.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Isa dito is yung in-extend po natin yung maturity nung allowable loans.

asr-001097
01:06:14.930 --> 01:06:20.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dati-rati, five years ang maximum nung pwedeng i-payroll deduction.

asr-001098
01:06:20.930 --> 01:06:22.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So hindi lumalampas ng five years.

asr-001099
01:06:22.930 --> 01:06:25.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sumulat po tayo sa BSP na i-extend po ito.

asr-001100
01:06:25.930 --> 01:06:27.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kaya pinayagan po ng BSP.

asr-001101
01:06:27.930 --> 01:06:28.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kaya seven years.

asr-001102
01:06:28.930 --> 01:06:31.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Binaba po nung maraming financial institution o banko,

asr-001103
01:06:31.930 --> 01:06:33.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ang nagbaba ng kanilang interest.

asr-001104
01:06:33.930 --> 01:06:34.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At tumagal din po yung payment.

asr-001105
01:06:34.930 --> 01:06:40.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Dahil makikita naman po natin, tumatagal din po ang ating mga teachers sa tenure nila.

asr-001106
01:06:40.930 --> 01:06:42.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Many stay 10, 20, 30 years.

asr-001107
01:06:42.930 --> 01:06:48.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So this is a more realistic option for them financially, Your Honor.

asr-001108
01:06:48.930 --> 01:06:49.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Madam Chair.

asr-001109
01:06:49.930 --> 01:06:57.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Lastly po, yung nabanggit kanina ni Kong Erice na 150 ba yung backlog niya.

asr-001110
01:06:57.930 --> 01:06:59.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Medyo naingit ako kasi yung sa amin 700 eh.

asr-001111
01:06:59.930 --> 01:07:00.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Madam Chair.

asr-001112
01:07:00.930 --> 01:07:06.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Hindi kaya pwedeng yung mga mas maraming kulang eh mas maraming ma-allocate na school buildings?

asr-001113
01:07:06.930 --> 01:07:13.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Kasi minsan naingit kami yung ibang tao na wala, ibang distrito na konting-konti lang pare-pareho kami ng allocation every year eh.

asr-001114
01:07:13.930 --> 01:07:15.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's a good point, Your Honor.

asr-001115
01:07:15.930 --> 01:07:19.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will look into that and we'll work with you on that, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

asr-001116
01:07:19.930 --> 01:07:21.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

asr-001117
01:07:21.930 --> 01:07:22.930
Rep. Adrian Michael A. Amatong: And good luck sa DepEd family.

asr-001118
01:07:22.930 --> 01:07:24.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming salamat sa suporta, Kong Adrian.

asr-001119
01:07:24.930 --> 01:07:25.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you po.

asr-001120
01:07:25.930 --> 01:07:27.930
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Thank you.

asr-001121
01:07:27.930 --> 01:07:29.930
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Next to ask question is from the minority.

asr-001122
01:07:29.930 --> 01:07:34.930
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The Chair acknowledges Representative Antonio L. Tinio.

asr-001123
01:07:34.930 --> 01:07:36.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001124
01:07:36.930 --> 01:07:40.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Good morning po sa DepEd, kay Secretary Angara.

asr-001125
01:07:40.930 --> 01:07:43.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Unang tanong tungkol po sa expanded career progression.

asr-001126
01:07:43.930 --> 01:07:48.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, from the field ang nakakarating po sa atin

asr-001127
01:07:48.930 --> 01:07:56.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng implementation and funding ng ECP 2025-2026.

asr-001128
01:07:56.930 --> 01:07:58.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilan pa po yung backlog?

asr-001129
01:07:58.930 --> 01:08:06.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ilan pa po yung backlog na qualified na pero hindi pa napopromote dahil walang budget?

asr-001130
01:08:06.930 --> 01:08:11.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor, Madam Chair, magandang umaga, Kong Tonjie.

asr-001131
01:08:11.930 --> 01:08:15.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: For 2026, there is a 6 billion budget given by Congress.

asr-001132
01:08:15.930 --> 01:08:22.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And this is enough to promote 82,000 of our teachers and school heads, Your Honor.

asr-001133
01:08:22.930 --> 01:08:25.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And in 2027, there is a 12 billion budget.

asr-001134
01:08:25.930 --> 01:08:30.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And this should answer for the promotions of 135,000 school heads.

asr-001135
01:08:30.930 --> 01:08:32.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, hindi po equal yung...

asr-001136
01:08:32.930 --> 01:08:35.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi yung minsan, sa tagal nang hindi sila napromote,

asr-001137
01:08:35.930 --> 01:08:39.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they are not only being promoted ng isang rangpo,

asr-001138
01:08:39.930 --> 01:08:41.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi minsan dalawa, tatlo.

asr-001139
01:08:41.930 --> 01:08:43.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, teacher 1, nagiging teacher 4.

asr-001140
01:08:43.930 --> 01:08:45.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Teacher 4, nagiging teacher...

asr-001141
01:08:45.930 --> 01:08:48.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We made new positions, Your Honor.

asr-001142
01:08:48.930 --> 01:08:50.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, teacher 6, gano'n minsan may gano'n.

asr-001143
01:08:50.930 --> 01:08:52.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hindi lang isang rangpo po.

asr-001144
01:08:52.930 --> 01:08:53.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, 82,000 promotions were...

asr-001145
01:08:53.930 --> 01:08:59.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 82,000 promotions were funded for 2026.

asr-001146
01:08:59.930 --> 01:09:00.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-001147
01:09:00.930 --> 01:09:04.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ilan yung nag-iintay pa ng funding?

asr-001148
01:09:04.930 --> 01:09:07.930
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Qualified na pero nag-iintay pa ng funding?

asr-001149
01:09:07.930 --> 01:09:17.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Mga, there are about 100,000 still waiting and entitled to the promotions, Your Honor.

asr-001150
01:09:17.250 --> 01:09:23.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, in other words, may qualified na sila, 100,000.

asr-001151
01:09:23.250 --> 01:09:26.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: They went through the process pero nag-iintay pa ng funding.

asr-001152
01:09:26.250 --> 01:09:27.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So...

asr-001153
01:09:28.250 --> 01:09:31.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kailan po sila mapupondohan?

asr-001154
01:09:31.250 --> 01:09:36.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: In 2027, Your Honor, because we only have 6 billion for this year, Your Honor.

asr-001155
01:09:36.250 --> 01:09:41.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, again, for 2027, ang target niyo po ay...

asr-001156
01:09:41.250 --> 01:09:43.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: That's good for...

asr-001157
01:09:43.250 --> 01:09:45.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: 135,000, Your Honor.

asr-001158
01:09:45.250 --> 01:09:51.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 135,000. So, yung 100,000 dun ay para lang dun sa backlog.

asr-001159
01:09:51.250 --> 01:09:52.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Opo.

asr-001160
01:09:52.250 --> 01:09:57.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in effect, for 2027, the new promotions will be for 35,000.

asr-001161
01:09:57.250 --> 01:09:58.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001162
01:09:58.250 --> 01:10:04.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. So, medyo maglilimit muna for 2027.

asr-001163
01:10:04.250 --> 01:10:08.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tama ho. Nag-ahabol talaga tayo dahil for many years, wala hong na-promote.

asr-001164
01:10:08.250 --> 01:10:13.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama naman po iyon. At mabuti po at napatutupad na ito.

asr-001165
01:10:13.250 --> 01:10:21.250
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Just a particular concern regarding headteachers.

asr-001166
01:10:21.250 --> 01:10:27.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: May mga headteacher na school head na nagpaabot sa atin.

asr-001167
01:10:27.530 --> 01:10:34.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nagpaabot sa atin na niri-reassign na sila away from being school heads.

asr-001168
01:10:34.530 --> 01:10:46.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Samantala, sa inyong guidelines, they have, I think, 2 years more na manatili sila at magpa-qualify bilang principal.

asr-001169
01:10:46.530 --> 01:10:53.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pwede po bang ma-reiterate yung policy na iyon? Kasi nga ang concern nila, ba't inaalis na sila?

asr-001170
01:10:53.530 --> 01:10:56.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Niri-reassign na sila from being school heads.

asr-001171
01:10:56.530 --> 01:11:03.530
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's purely voluntary, I believe, Your Honor. And they're allowed 2 years. That's what the law provides, Your Honor.

asr-001172
01:11:03.530 --> 01:11:14.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero meron nga mga divisions na nagpaabot sa amin na involuntarily niri-reassign sila or may banta na niri-reassign na sila.

asr-001173
01:11:14.530 --> 01:11:17.530
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We will reiterate the policy, Your Honor.

asr-001174
01:11:17.530 --> 01:11:23.530
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, please. Dahil nagpaabot po iyong mga headteachers. Okay.

