03:50:51.950 --> 03:50:52.770
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Siguro ang kasabay natin

asr-003447
03:50:52.890 --> 03:50:54.790
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Indonesia, Cambodia.

asr-003448
03:50:54.790 --> 03:50:54.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah.

asr-003449
03:50:56.050 --> 03:50:56.590
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Nasa ilalim naman natin

asr-003450
03:50:56.590 --> 03:50:59.270
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung Laos and Myanmar, Your Honor.

asr-003451
03:50:59.950 --> 03:51:00.210
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah.

asr-003452
03:51:00.470 --> 03:51:02.550
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in short, we are...

asr-003453
03:51:02.550 --> 03:51:05.350
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: if not on top, at least at par in the middle.

asr-003454
03:51:05.770 --> 03:51:08.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're in the middle, but hopefully we can...

asr-003455
03:51:08.390 --> 03:51:10.990
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: I think we have the potential to do better, Your Honor.

asr-003456
03:51:11.230 --> 03:51:11.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah.

asr-003457
03:51:11.770 --> 03:51:14.890
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Chair, Secretary, what do you think, you know,

asr-003458
03:51:15.290 --> 03:51:16.590
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: on the onset, what do you think,

asr-003459
03:51:16.810 --> 03:51:18.230
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: at least we have...

asr-003460
03:51:18.230 --> 03:51:19.410
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We cannot beat Singapore.

asr-003461
03:51:19.530 --> 03:51:20.310
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: We know that.

asr-003462
03:51:20.390 --> 03:51:21.510
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's a given.

asr-003463
03:51:21.930 --> 03:51:24.330
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: But at least, even if we're in the middle,

asr-003464
03:51:24.330 --> 03:51:26.090
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: what do you think we need to do?

asr-003465
03:51:26.590 --> 03:51:28.090
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: As a nation, no?

asr-003466
03:51:28.230 --> 03:51:32.130
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Hindi naman lahat kayang gawin ng DepEd.

asr-003467
03:51:32.350 --> 03:51:34.130
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It is a whole-nation approach.

asr-003468
03:51:34.310 --> 03:51:36.770
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What do you think we need to do as a nation?

asr-003469
03:51:37.130 --> 03:51:38.510
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ang tinitingnan ko ho yung Vietnam.

asr-003470
03:51:38.770 --> 03:51:41.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi dati nauunahan ho natin ang Vietnam,

asr-003471
03:51:42.050 --> 03:51:44.650
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: pero ngayon nalampasan na ho tayo, especially sa test scores.

asr-003472
03:51:45.190 --> 03:51:48.590
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: They focus on certain points.

asr-003473
03:51:49.410 --> 03:51:51.190
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Number one is the budgetary allocation.

asr-003474
03:51:51.370 --> 03:51:54.710
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: They spend 20% of their national budget for education.

asr-003475
03:51:54.710 --> 03:51:55.710
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And they...

asr-003476
03:51:56.590 --> 03:52:00.110
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: They pay a particular focus on teachers and teacher training, Your Honor.

asr-003477
03:52:00.310 --> 03:52:09.630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So they make sure that their teachers are satisfied,

asr-003478
03:52:09.630 --> 03:52:11.070
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: at may magandang career path.

asr-003479
03:52:11.510 --> 03:52:14.030
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So talagang promotion, further studies ng teachers nila.

asr-003480
03:52:14.530 --> 03:52:15.730
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Inaalagaan talaga nila.

asr-003481
03:52:16.350 --> 03:52:18.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: They focus on strengthening their teachers.

asr-003482
03:52:19.010 --> 03:52:24.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi alam nila na yan ang heart, as our President said,

asr-003483
03:52:24.390 --> 03:52:25.870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: of the educational system.

asr-003484
03:52:26.030 --> 03:52:26.390
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I think...

asr-003485
03:52:26.590 --> 03:52:32.310
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I think those are two strong points that we can borrow from Vietnam.

asr-003486
03:52:32.310 --> 03:52:35.750
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa Indonesia, meron din silang app para sa teachers.

asr-003487
03:52:35.750 --> 03:52:38.710
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So may feedback mechanism with teachers.

asr-003488
03:52:38.710 --> 03:52:46.590
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Of course, Singapore, Thailand, Malaysia, they invest a lot in education, Your Honor,

asr-003489
03:52:46.590 --> 03:52:49.830
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: especially early child care, Your Honor.

asr-003490
03:52:49.830 --> 03:52:52.550
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Chair, of course, to the Secretary.

asr-003491
03:52:52.550 --> 03:52:55.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You mentioned that in Vietnam, usually Vietnam.

asr-003492
03:52:55.430 --> 03:52:56.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yes.

asr-003493
03:52:56.430 --> 03:53:02.630
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Noong early seventies, eighties, pumupunta sila sa atin para pag-aralan ang farming natin, di ba?

asr-003494
03:53:02.850 --> 03:53:03.750
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ngayon, baligtad na.

asr-003495
03:53:04.030 --> 03:53:05.470
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mas marami na silang napo-produce kaysa sa atin.

asr-003496
03:53:05.470 --> 03:53:11.510
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And then, when it comes to education, 20% of the total national budget.

asr-003497
03:53:12.110 --> 03:53:15.410
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, right now, we have something like 7.2 trillion.

asr-003498
03:53:15.910 --> 03:53:19.630
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I think it is only right na yung 20% to achieve.

asr-003499
03:53:20.030 --> 03:53:24.030
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember, laging sinasabi ng mga bayani natin,

asr-003500
03:53:24.190 --> 03:53:27.550
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: kabataan ang pag-asa ng kinabukasan natin.

asr-003506
03:53:27.550 --> 03:53:31.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I think this is the high time po na 20% is not bad.

asr-003507
03:53:31.810 --> 03:53:37.890
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Right now, ilang percent po ang pie natin sa budget natin?

asr-003508
03:53:38.190 --> 03:53:38.730
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ilang percent?

asr-003509
03:53:39.250 --> 03:53:43.130
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's about 14% of the, 14.3% of the national budget.

asr-003510
03:53:44.030 --> 03:53:45.190
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That's the budget.

asr-003511
03:53:45.490 --> 03:53:45.630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Yeah.

asr-003512
03:53:45.910 --> 03:53:46.410
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So ang baba, no?

asr-003513
03:53:47.350 --> 03:53:48.050
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Hindi naman mababa yun.

asr-003514
03:53:48.530 --> 03:53:50.750
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Medyo maganda na 'yan kumpara sa dati, Your Honor.

asr-003515
03:53:50.750 --> 03:53:54.730
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero I think we should be conscious about moving it towards a certain goal.

asr-003516
03:53:54.730 --> 03:53:55.190
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah.

asr-003517
03:53:55.390 --> 03:53:56.270
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: You're being modest.

asr-003518
03:53:56.430 --> 03:53:59.010
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Secretary. Pero actually, no?

asr-003519
03:53:59.010 --> 03:54:01.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi when you look at Vietnam, nakikita ko,

asr-003520
03:54:01.800 --> 03:54:06.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: of course, Japan, Korea, malalayo na 'yan. Mas marami na rin silang computer, eh.

asr-003521
03:54:06.100 --> 03:54:10.950
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In our ratio po natin sa ating mga schools,

asr-003522
03:54:10.950 --> 03:54:16.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: per school, per ano, hindi na per student, per school class na lang po.

asr-003523
03:54:16.200 --> 03:54:22.150
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ilan po ang?are we behind when it comes to computers po para sa learning ng ating mga estudyante?

asr-003524
03:54:22.150 --> 03:54:25.400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Medyo ho nahuli ho tayo diyan.

asr-003526
03:54:25.400 --> 03:54:32.110
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But the goal is really to have at least one computer lab in each school, Your Honor, para at least may optimum na setup.

asr-003527
03:54:32.110 --> 03:54:36.190
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: there's such a thing as too much computer time also actually that's a new finding now

asr-003528
03:54:36.190 --> 03:54:45.070
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That is why many countries, like the Nordic countries, bumabalik na po sa pen and paper actually, because dati one gadget, one learner sila, but hindi na po iyon ang standard ngayon.

asr-003529
03:54:45.070 --> 03:54:48.270
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: they're limiting the computer used to one to three hours a week

asr-003530
03:54:48.270 --> 03:54:50.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: so that is attainable in my opinion uh

asr-003531
03:54:50.430 --> 03:55:05.310
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: sa atin. Basta consistent tayo sa purchasing of our computers for the computer labs. And yun po ang importante po, dahil sa PISA, if you read the PISA report of 2018 and 2022,

asr-003532
03:55:05.310 --> 03:55:10.350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: many the feedback was that many of our learners were not familiar with digital technology

asr-003533
03:55:10.350 --> 03:55:20.430
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And it was the first time that they encountered using a mouse during the exam itself. Kaya itong nahuling PISA exam noong 2025, sinigurado natin lahat na kukuha ng

asr-003534
03:55:20.430 --> 03:55:30.990
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: exam, at least makaramdam na gumamit ng computer. Hindi sila manibago dahil sayang yung oras nila pag doon nila kakabisaduhin yung paggamit ng computer.

asr-003535
03:55:30.990 --> 03:55:34.990
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Madam Chair, thank you, Madam Chair. So yun nga, tama si Secretary na

asr-003536
03:55:37.470 --> 03:55:42.510
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: at least one computer per classroom. I hope it is going to be achievable.

asr-003537
03:55:44.110 --> 03:55:44.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Pagdating sa internet

asr-003538
03:55:44.430 --> 03:55:51.900
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: connectivity natin, ano naman po ang ratio natin?

asr-003539
03:55:51.900 --> 03:56:03.820
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Mga 19% lang ho ang schools?99% tayo may internet. 99 pala, sorry, 99%. Pero yung importanteng point diyan is yung ibang mababa po ang bandwidth.

asr-003540
03:56:03.820 --> 03:56:13.250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: so we're trying to get to at least uh so there are 460 schools without internet

asr-003541
03:56:13.970 --> 03:56:16.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Having said that, yung quality ng internet is variable.

asr-003542
03:56:18.210 --> 03:56:24.130
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Sa iba, sa opisina lang ng principal may internet. So I guess the next goal is to aim for greater bandwidth in schools, so that you are able to

asr-003543
03:56:24.130 --> 03:56:24.370
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: use

asr-003544
03:56:24.690 --> 03:56:28.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: things like academy uh and other education software your honor

asr-003545
03:56:30.530 --> 03:56:35.970
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Madam Chair. Secretary, I do not know if someone asked this question:

asr-003546
03:56:35.970 --> 03:56:38.050
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: how do we integrate AI ngayon?

asr-003547
03:56:41.410 --> 03:56:42.450
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi mukhang sabi nga ni Elon [unclear], in the next five years daw,

asr-003548
03:56:44.210 --> 03:56:47.810
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: human robotics will be more intelligent than humans.

asr-003549
03:56:48.370 --> 03:56:53.570
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Paano tayo mag-cope up in the next few years when it comes to AI?

asr-003550
03:56:54.210 --> 03:56:59.810
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: May upside and downside po ang AI. So I think on the upside it can really help our teachers upskill,

asr-003551
03:56:59.810 --> 03:57:04.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: especially when EDCOM has reported a skills mismatch, meaning yung nagtuturo ng science

asr-003552
03:57:04.850 --> 03:57:08.050
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi pala science teacher, yung nagtuturo ng chemistry

asr-003553
03:57:09.490 --> 03:57:16.690
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi naman pala expert sa chemistry. So yung mga ganon, I think AI can really help assist, and also yung personalized learning,

asr-003554
03:57:17.250 --> 03:57:21.970
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: each learner can proceed at their own speed. So iyon ang upside ng AI. The downside is that there are

asr-003555
03:57:21.970 --> 03:57:23.410
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: studies which show that uh

asr-003556
03:57:23.570 --> 03:57:30.930
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ai can in very young children or in younger children ai can diminish the creative thinking and

asr-003557
03:57:30.930 --> 03:57:39.650
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: the critical faculties of our learners. So iyon ang babalansehin ho natin. You have to introduce it at the right age and

asr-003558
03:57:39.650 --> 03:57:44.850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: with the right safeguards uh and of course we must train our teachers to use it appropriately your

asr-003559
03:57:44.850 --> 03:57:46.200
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

